            "caption": "",
            "heading": "",
            "text": "<p>The world has lost its way with water. <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/29673-how-much-water-on-earth.html\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Less than 1 %</strong> </a>of the earth’s freshwater is actually accessible and <a href=\"https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/story/globally-3-billion-people-health-risk-due-scarce-data-water-quality\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>over three billion people</strong> </a>in the world are at risk of disease because their water quality is unknown. <a href=\"https://www.statista.com/topics/5401/global-plastic-waste/#topicOverview\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Almost 400 million tonnes of plastic are produced globally per year</strong>. </a>In the UK alone, <a href=\"https://www.london.gov.uk/programmes-strategies/environment-and-climate-change/waste-and-recycling/single-use-plastic-bottles\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>7.7 billion plastic water bottles</strong> </a>are bought each year - many of which end up <a href=\"https://www.iucn.org/resources/issues-brief/marine-plastic-pollution#:~:text=Over%20300%20million%20tons%20of,waters%20to%20deep%2Dsea%20sediments.\" target=\"_blank\">i<strong>n the ocean.</strong></a></p>",
